"\nTARGET 37 docs/work\u002dlogs/2026_08\u002dwork_logs/2026_08_28\u002dwork_log.md bounded\u002dday\u002dentry\nIDENTITY 835f097fc480122fb39c519ae94ee5c06ddcf2db d0f44bbe3b6f290bc450065a4a03261da6398060bcd69d3037f83741cb853d36 RANGES [[142, 231]] MASKED [170, 175, 194, 195, 225]\n142: ## 20:40 UTC \u2014 Cloud setup: the SSH flow is the wrong shape; native setup designed and started\n143: \n144: ### What the device QA actually found\n145: \n146: Setting up a Dropbox remote through the shipped wizard failed at four points,\n147: against a person who had written the instructions himself:\n148: \n149: 1. **rclone's prompt contradicts ours.** At `Use auto config?` rclone says\n150:    *\"Say N if running rclone on a (remote) machine without web browser\n151:    access\"* \u2014 which describes the handheld exactly. N is fatal here. rclone's\n152:    advice is in the terminal at the decision point; ours is on another screen,\n153:    on another device, several steps earlier. **Ours loses that contest every\n154:    time.** Naming a conflicting instruction beats restating our own.\n155: 2. **Answering N collides on port 53682** \u2014 `rclone authorize` cannot bind it\n156:    because the SSH tunnel holds it, then floods `channel 3: open failed`.\n157: 3. **\"Failed to open browser automatically\" prints on every run** (no browser\n158:    on the device) and reads as an error at the moment the player must act.\n159: 4. **The auth link exists only in terminal scrollback.** Our step said \"sign in\n160:    via the link in your browser\", implying one opens by itself.\n161: \n162: All four are us documenting a hostile interface. Fixed the text\n163: (`feature/cloud\u002dsetup\u002dpolish`), but the fix is the wrong altitude.\n164: \n165: ### The unlock\n166: \n167: `rclone config create <name> <type> key=value` writes a remote\n168: non\u002dinteractively, `\u002d\u002dnon\u002dinteractive` is documented as being *\"for use by\n169: applications that wish to configure rclone themselves\"*, and every OAuth\n170: [MASKED sensitive\u002dlabelled line; not read unredacted]\n171: change is needed** \u2014 we perform the grant and hand rclone the result. Issue\n172: #29 reframed accordingly.\n173: \n174: Backend tiering, from `rclone config providers` on the device (69 backends):\n175: [MASKED sensitive\u002dlabelled line; not read unredacted]\n176: with no redirect_uri; drive + onedrive via device flow), **16 SSH fallback**.\n177: \n178: ### We register no OAuth clients \u2014 decided, with reasons\n179: \n180: The maintainer pushed back on ROCKNIX holding OAuth registrations. Correct on\n181: principle, and the practice is worse than the principle:\n182: \n183: \u002d An unverified Google app is capped at **100 users**, and Testing status\n184:   **invalidates refresh tokens after 7 days** \u2014 weekly re\u002dauth for everyone.\n185: \u002d rclone is already retiring its shared Drive client_id (\"will stop working\n186:   during 2026\"), so Drive is going bring\u002dyour\u002down regardless.\n187: \n188: Player supplies their own client_id; we make everything after that painless.\n189: 50 of 69 backends are unaffected because they involve no OAuth at all.\n190: \n191: ### Non\u002dobvious things worth keeping\n192: \n193: \u002d **rclone's own metadata cannot decide input masking.** `sftp.host` is\n194: [MASKED sensitive\u002dlabelled line; not read unredacted]\n195: [MASKED sensitive\u002dlabelled line; not read unredacted]\n196:   Report both flags and let the UI decide (settled: mask either, reveal on\n197:   open \u2014 which ES already does, since the row masks but the editor gets\n198:   plaintext).\n199: \u002d **ES wizard pages cannot scroll.** `ComponentList` moves the camera from\n200:   `mCursor` (ComponentList.cpp:299) and cursor movement skips unselectable\n201:   rows (ComponentList.h:120). A page of info/prose rows has no selectable row\n202:   at all, so content past the fold is *unreachable*, not merely off\u002dscreen.\n203:   Text on those pages has a hard height budget.\n204: \u002d **`ComponentList` insets selectable rows only** \u2014 an unselectable row sits\n205:   flush at x=0 while group headers and value rows are at 10px, so prose rows\n206:   must pad themselves.\n207: \u002d `rclone` already depends on **qrencode**, so QR generation for a phone\n208:   hand\u002doff is available today.\n209: \n210: ### Process failure worth naming\n211: \n212: Diagnosing \"SSH times out\" I asserted **wireless client isolation**, retracted\n213: it on a sweep that looked random, then re\u002dderived it, then had it broken again\n214: by \"wired doesn't work either\" \u2014 before the real cause turned out to be stale\n215: Orbi 970 bridge state that a router reboot cleared.\n216: \n217: The sweep only looked random because I had not established **which hosts were\n218: wireless**. The rule: *establish the classifying variable before asserting or\n219: withdrawing a cause.* Also, `ip neigh` showing `FAILED` settles layer 2 in one\n220: command and should come before any port scan; and \"what makes the one working\n221: host different?\" was the question all along \u2014 I treated serval as an exception\n222: to explain away rather than the evidence.\n223: \n224: Filed: #51 (native remote setup), #52 (rclone.conf missing from backuptool's\n225: [MASKED sensitive\u002dlabelled line; not read unredacted]\n226: remote is hard, which #51 exists to change).\n227: \n228: Built: `cloud_remote` (97b3ee5475) \u2014 providers/fields/create/list, verified on\n229: the H700. Refuses to modify an existing remote; verifies with `rclone lsd`\n230: before reporting success and rolls back if that fails.\n\nTARGET 38 docs/work\u002dlogs/2026_08\u002dwork_logs/2026_08_29\u002dwork_log.md bounded\u002dday\u002dentry\nIDENTITY 1d31599aea4681c7eebfe348c76f2c3dc0cfd6af b7b8c124192bb5319ea99824ebb6148ff89894de6ab3bf85330c6e306acd73c0 RANGES [[231, 263]] MASKED []\n231: ## 23:20 UTC \u2014 Second Dropbox test: the box that looked filled in\n232: \n233: Same outcome, different cause, and a worse one because it was ours to see.\n234: \n235: The paste field carried `placeholder=\"http://localhost:53682/?code=...\"`. Grey\n236: hint text reads as a value \u2014 the tester pressed the button on what looked like\n237: a completed form, got \"That did not contain a code\", and stopped. A placeholder\n238: that shows the *shape of the value* rather than *the instruction* is a trap\n239: (D\u002dUI\u002d007); every one on this flow now says what to do.\n240: \n241: Around it: the button says **Confirm** rather than Finish; an empty submit says\n242: nothing was pasted and where to get it; **pasting submits on its own**, since\n243: the two minutes the address lives are exactly what gets spent hunting for the\n244: button; the note names the error the phone actually shows (\"this site can't be\n245: reached\") instead of describing it; and **\"Lost the address? Start over\"** is\n246: permanently on the page, so the flow has no state with no way forward.\n247: \n248: Two structural simplifications from the same round of feedback:\n249: \n250: \u002d **One cloud entry.** `SET UP CLOUD REMOTE` and `CONNECT CLOUD STORAGE` named\n251:   the same job, and the first opened the SSH wizard the second replaced. Now\n252:   `USE A COMPUTER INSTEAD`, one level down \u2014 rclone's own config is still the\n253:   only route to a crypt/union remote or a reconnect (D\u002dUI\u002d005). The\n254:   post\u002drestore message that named the old entry went with it, per the\n255:   menu\u002dmoved rule in `upgrade\u002dand\u002dinstall.md`.\n256: \u002d **The PIN is the tail of the address.** `http://device:8080/7677`, and the QR\n257:   encodes the same string, so the handheld shows one line and the typed path\n258:   needs nothing extra (D\u002dUI\u002d006).\n259: \n260: Checked and rejected: an out\u002dof\u002dband flow that would remove the dead redirect\n261: altogether. `rclone authorize` only offers the loopback\u002dserver flow \u2014 no\n262: provider\u002ddisplayed code \u2014 so the dead page stands (D\u002dCLOUD\u002d012).\n\nTARGET 39 docs/work\u002dlogs/2026_08\u002dwork_logs/2026_08_30\u002dwork_log.md bounded\u002dday\u002dentry\nIDENTITY 615c4803f00275aa387f6b3a03dad428206b2fa7 763f6fa3f87455428a40b04caf5808e14fa6c35960748e92ad13cfee2741c695 RANGES [[3, 45]] MASKED []\n3: ## 00:35 UTC \u2014 Why the redirect cannot come back to us, and a CSS escape that shipped\n4: \n5: **The redirect question, settled with evidence.** The maintainer asked why the\n6: provider sends the phone to `localhost:53682` rather than the device's IP.\n7: Checked on the device rather than reasoned about:\n8: \n9: ```\n10: $ cloud_oauth info | sed \u002dn 's/^PROVIDER=//p' | tr '&' '\\n' | grep redirect\n11: redirect_uri=http%3A%2F%2Flocalhost%3A53682%2F\n12: ```\n13: \n14: That value is fixed by what rclone registered with Dropbox for its client id.\n15: `rclone help flags | grep \u002di redirect` offers nothing \u2014 the `\u002d\u002d*\u002dauth\u002durl`\n16: flags change the *auth server*, not the redirect. The binary does carry\n17: `urn:ietf:wg:oauth:2.0:oob` and `https://oauth.rclone.org/`, but neither is a\n18: LAN address (the latter is rclone's own shim, which itself redirects to\n19: `http://localhost:53682/`). And `192.168.1.81:8080` could never be registered:\n20: it is different on every network. So the dead page stands \u2014 D\u002dCLOUD\u002d012 holds,\n21: now with the check behind it rather than an argument.\n22: \n23: **A CSS escape that survived a move.** Pulling the stylesheet into a `STYLE`\n24: constant broke it. The page templates use `%`\u002dformatting, so their inline CSS\n25: had to write `%%`; moved into a constant that is substituted *as a value*\n26: (`%(style)s`), the formatter never descends into it and `width:100%%` shipped\n27: as literal CSS. Browsers discard an invalid declaration without complaint and\n28: render the page, so three dead rules \u2014 both text inputs and every button \u2014\n29: were invisible.\n30: \n31: The visible symptom was the one reported: a four\u002dcharacter PIN box rendering at\n32: its default twenty\u002dcharacter width, which with 24px type and half\u002dem letter\n33: spacing overflows the card on a phone. Filed as blindspot 19, because the\n34: general shape (escaping that was right where the text used to live) will\n35: recur, and because the guard is specific: assert on the rendered output, not\n36: on the fact that it rendered.\n37: \n38: **Also:** the phone page is two numbered steps in the order they happen (sign\n39: in, then paste), reversing the paste\u002dbox\u002dfirst arrangement from yesterday \u2014\n40: that was right when the button was being mistaken for the whole job, and\n41: numbering makes the natural order read better. And the handheld's sign\u002din page\n42: gained a spacer under the group rule, which ComponentList draws flush against\n43: whatever follows; everywhere else that is text with its own leading, here it\n44: was a QR.\n\nTARGET 40 docs/work\u002dlogs/2026_08\u002dwork_logs/2026_08_31\u002dwork_log.md bounded\u002dday\u002dentry\nIDENTITY 96b34d7abcba69b6e490b8fb683fcaf6463dcb66 f008c53c61367c472df6500ae8e4b1295c512ee1aed33e50f35dc8eac471993b RANGES [[293, 331]] MASKED [295, 296]\n293: ## 2026\u002d09\u002d01 01:10 UTC \u2014 A pointer, and a field that can be selected\n294: \n295: [MASKED sensitive\u002dlabelled line; not read unredacted]\n296: [MASKED sensitive\u002dlabelled line; not read unredacted]\n297: a page and leaves focus on the body, so nothing holds the caret \u002d\u002d the\n298: on\u002dscreen keyboard has nowhere to type and spatial navigation has no anchor\n299: to move from. The focus poll now adopts a visible text field when the page\n300: has abandoned focus, never when something else holds it.\n301: \n302: And the virtual pointer, one round after filing #55 for it. Built as a\n303: **uinput device** rather than a cursor drawn by the window: sway renders it,\n304: WebKit gets real pointer events, and it therefore reaches the two overlays\n305: that were covering most of a four\u002dinch screen \u002d\u002d including Google's One Tap\n306: prompt, which is a cross\u002dorigin iframe no focus traversal can enter. Dragged\n307: from a trackpad area on the phone page, which is where the touchscreen is.\n308: \n309: Proof it delivers: a synthesised click moved page focus from BUTTON to BODY.\n310: \n311: Two findings from testing it:\n312: \n313: \u002d libinput applies pointer acceleration, so a delta of N does not move N\n314:   pixels. Fine for a person watching the cursor; it means a script cannot\n315:   drive the pointer by dead reckoning, which cost an hour of \"the click is\n316:   not landing\" before the BUTTON\u002d>BODY transition showed that it was.\n317: \u002d `seat * hide_cursor 1000` is in ROCKNIX's sway config. Right for a handheld\n318:   with no mouse, wrong while one is being dragged \u002d\u002d the pointer disappears a\n319:   second after movement stops and the tap is aimed blind. Disabled for the\n320:   window's lifetime.\n321: \n322: Also: the phone's typing box now keeps what was typed. Clearing it after\n323: every keystroke made a keyboard that looked broken \u002d\u002d you type and nothing\n324: appears anywhere you can see. Only the difference is sent, through a promise\n325: queue so characters cannot overtake each other and arrive scrambled.\n326: \n327: **Unverified:** the phone\u002ddriven feel. Driven synthetically over SSH, never\n328: by a finger on a phone against the handheld's screen.\n329: \n330: Image `117f618f\u2026` staged and hash\u002dverified.\n\nTARGET 41 docs/work\u002dlogs/2026_09\u002dwork_logs/2026_09_01\u002dwork_log.md bounded\u002dday\u002dentry\nIDENTITY 18de47e528035225bc358b6920e73a6ae264f791 7bc98a01c7ed8ca44a8c9214f9a0a47a24d8a88462eae5bfd7168fb00579652c RANGES [[152, 193]] MASKED []\n152: ## 19:20 UTC \u2014 VM testing, and the three bugs it found\n153: \n154: Run against the local WebDAV backend, seeded as a second handheld: two GBA\n155: saves, a savestate, a screenshot and its own system archive. The scenario\n156: that cost 70 files this afternoon, reproduced where it costs nothing.\n157: \n158: | Test | Result |\n159: | \u002d\u002d\u002d | \u002d\u002d\u002d |\n160: | `copy` preserves another device's saves | 5 survived, merged to 7 |\n161: | `sync` archives rather than destroys | moved to `/GAMES\u002dreplaced/<date>/` |\n162: | `sync` leaves the backup folder alone | survives (after the fix below) |\n163: | the `sync` \u002d> `copy` rewrite is one\u002dtime | a deliberate `sync` is respected |\n164: \n165: ### Three bugs, none of them findable by reading\n166: \n167: **`\u002d\u002ddelete\u002dexcluded` was deleting every device's system backup.** In sync\n168: mode the saves phase removes whatever the allowlist does not admit, and the\n169: backup folder is deliberately excluded \u002d\u002d so it was carried off, and the\n170: phase that follows re\u002duploaded only this device's. `cloud_restore` has\n171: stripped that flag since issue #5, with a comment saying backup could keep it\n172: because it only tidies the remote. The remote holds every handheld's backups.\n173: The premise was wrong and had been written down as reasoning.\n174: \n175: **My own `sync` \u002d> `copy` rewrite was a veto, not a migration.** It ran on\n176: every backup, so a deliberately set mirror came back as copy on the next run.\n177: Anybody who read the docs and chose one would have been overruled for ever.\n178: Marker\u002dgated now.\n179: \n180: **`/GAMES` was displayed as `/GAME`.** `Utils::Platform::GetShOutput` drops\n181: the last character of what it reads, and the command used `echo \u002dn`, so there\n182: was no trailing newline to lose instead. Blindspot 3, recurring in code we\n183: wrote, and visible only in a screenshot of the menu.\n184: \n185: ### What that says about the last few rounds\n186: \n187: All three were in code already shipped to the device this afternoon. Two of\n188: them I had introduced today while fixing a data\u002dloss bug. Testing before\n189: shipping would have caught all three; D\u002dQA\u002d001 says VM verification gates the\n190: device build and several rounds went straight to hardware without it.\n191: \n192: Image `edd531e2\u2026` staged and hash\u002dverified.\n"
